      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-03-01_WidnesExaminer_art0013" n="art0013">
        <p>LANCASHIRE COUNTY ASYLUM, WINWICK, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>The VISITING COMMITTEE invite TENDERS for the supply of the under-mentioned goods, commencing Ist April next. FOR 12 MONTHS :- 1 Ale and Stout 21 Margarine 2 Attendants' Uniforms 22 Men's and Boys' Suits 3 Boots, Shoes &amp; Slippers 23 Necessaries 4 Brushes 24 Oils and Wax 5 Calico &amp; General Drapery 25 Paints 6 Cattle Cake 26 Paint Brushes 7 Cloth Caps 27 Poultry 8 Clothing ' 28 Preserves 9 Coffee and Chicory 29 Provender 10 Crockery 30 Smallwa:es 11 Fish 31 Soap and Soda 12 German Yeast 32 Sceks and Stockings 13 Glass 33 Timber 14 Grains 34 Tinned Beef &amp; Milk 15 Groceries (No. 1) 35 Tinwate 16 Groceries (No. 21 36 Tobacco and Snuff 17 Haberdashery 37 Tuning and Repairing 18 Indiarubber Goods Pianos 19 Leather and Grindery 38 Wines and Spirits 20 Linen Drapery 39 Woollen Drapery FOR 6 MONTHS. 40 Flour and Oatmeal 41 Provisions 42 Tea Tenders must be made on forms, which can be obtained from the undersigned before or during the time the kample a are on view, and must be delivered at the Asylum ncc later than 9 a.m. on the 10th March. Samples oi those goods, which must be accoiding to the Asylum samples, can be seen at the Asylum between 10 a.m. and 12 noon and 2 and 4 p.m. on the following days, viz., 21st, 24t1 and 25th February. Samples can NOT be seen after the 25th February, nor on any other dates than the above. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender, and reserve the right to accept or reject the whole or any part of a Tender. By Ord( r. P. IRVING DUTTON, 14th February, 1913. Clerk and Steward.</p>
      </div>
