      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-03-01_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <p>The Hull team is: E Rogers, full back; Francis, Gilbert, J P Smith and Nolan, threequarters ; G ,I°Rers and Andersen, half backs; Herridge, Holder, Yaylor, Merry, Allen and Darnaody, forwards. This Is a pretty hot combination and much will depend on the Warrington men securing the mastery in the pack.</p>
        <p>Their cup-tie opponents of next Saturday are at konie to Wakefield a match which should give War- Ilnyton a good ides of current form. Last Saturday. h.-eighley drew at Bradford 10-10, which was a 6nfficiently go, d performance to indicate that Warring- ton will have a stiff task to win at Lawkholuie-lane.</p>
        <p>The League table up-to-date is as follows : For. Agst. Per- P. W. L. D. G. T. P. G. T. P. c'nt'ge. nd'field —.26 03 3 0... 83137 577...30 32 156... 8846 b"igatt oughton 23 15 4 4... 40 55 245...13 24 98.. 73 91 "ewsbory 27 19 7 1... 57108 438...36 40 192... 72 22 11 K.R.25 17 7 1... 67 78 368...40 48 224... 7000 Salford Hunslet .. . Virakefield 1.26 16 8 2... 39 73 297...42 62 270... 653 g 9aldharn teleY I.eds .26 14 11 1 48 57 267.. 38 55 241... 5576 ra B dford 26 13 11 2... 34 40 188...31 52 218... 53.84 Svrin 24 12 11 1... 32 44 196...22 43 173... 52.08 27uhl ll 13 3... 28 40 176.. 38 68 280... 46 29 Widnes 26 11 13 2... 40 66 278...50 61 283... 46*15 St Helen 9 26 11 14 1... 47 72 310...41 57 253... 44.23 Whdale H 25 10 13 2... 31 59 239...31 42 188... 4400 Warrington 25 10 13 2... 31 34 164...30 49 207... 41 00 lialifax 26 816 2... 29 47 199...53 69 313... 34.61 Leigh 02 715 0... 15 99 117...34 53 227... 31 81 Runcorn 23 617 0... 26 32 148...44 74 310... 2608 ,Nrork 14ftrrow 23 5 17 1... 19 42 164...44 68 292... 2391 bßeighley 2l 315 3... 19 24 110...50 72 316... 21.42 granaley 94 419 1... 22 29 131...55116 458... 18.75 `4oventry 22 021 1... 24 31 141...95163 679... 2.27</p>
        <p>The men who greatly distinguished themselves at .111ferd were Jolley, who played a magnificent iefe.nsive game, Tranter and Brooks. The latter !gain showed great dash in the second half and seems '0 have recovered his best form</p>
        <p>---- liere at Warrington, the " A " triumphed in good ,r4tYle against Salford " A." Bardsley pleased the .:rowd with his keenness and dash, though he was °fie to get offside. He would be better with a thPeedier centre than Jordan, who runs across too IVIell• One run down touch which Bardsley made ear the end of the game indicated that he has the tnak• , ing of a really fine wing three-quarter. He has p.tri, pace and swerve, which most of our wings since I'4lB day have conspicuously lacked. Blundell, the F'dier forward, again played a dashing game, while 4e two Browns were both good in the back division. - There is no" A" team match to-day.</p>
        <p>TO-DAY'S MATCHES. tc, The following is a list of fixtures for to-day, ittagpther with the results of the corresponding games tiot season : hk,Tilet ktderstleld Vol:alley 23 Wakeflald Trinity ... 5 be,k 714.3blutly 21 Oldham. 11 ,7.,yar,r‘oo Rangers l3 Rochdale Hornets ... 2 11,411 .),.."ton ,nigegston R — Coventry ttarieZ • ...................... 16 Salford teigh . r 4 . 6 Swinton 2 .......................... ,-- Leeds —</p>
