        <p>COUNTY COUNCIL ELECTION. MAY Tru, 1913 TO THE ELECTORS OF WIDNES SOUTH DIVISION. DEAR SIR OR MADAM, A number of influential electors of South Widnes have asked rue to becoma the representative to the Lancashire County Council, and I have decided to offer my services to the electors as a whole. I have as your near neignbour been engaged for thirty years in industry, and have a material and social interest in your borough. I have leisure to devote myself to the work, and should you elect me I can promise to give to the interests of the County, ani especially to those of Widnes, my best attention. I have for long taken an active interest in public affairs, and have had considerable experience on various public bodies. In national affairs I am a Liberal, but it would be my desire, it elected to the County Council, to judge every question on its merits, and to represent the interests of the whole constituency without reference to party or creed. The work of the County Council is of considerable importance to all Lancashire people. It is concerned with such important subjects as Public Health, Allotments and Small Holdings, Roads, Waterways, Lunacy, Elementary Education in the County, Secondary Education in the Boroughs, &amp;c.. in Boroughs like Widnes the management of local affairs largely devolves upon local Councils, but there is no subject engaging the attention of the County Council in which all who reside and work in the County are not Interested. In addition the County Council have certain powers and joint interests with the Borough Authority, such as in Secondary Education, Roads, &amp;0., which directly affect Boroughs like Widnes. 1 offer to you the best services I can give. It is for you to express your acceptance or otherwise of those services upon the polling day. I am, Yours respectfully, CHARLES E. PARKER.</p>
