        <p>TO FIGHT SOCIALISM. The Earl of Wemyss, the first president, has headed with .£5OO a list of subscriptions to raise a fund of £20,000 for the organisation of Independent Political Associations to fight Socialism. A POSTMAN'S TENIPTATIONS. Edgar Partridge, a temporary postman, who was sent to trial at Coventry on Thursday, on a charge of stealing two 14s postal orders, said his last employer had not stamped his insurance card for eight weeks, and he could get no employment. When taken on by the Post Office at 18s. a week he succumbed to temptation In his bedroom were found 120 opened packets, some containing cheques and val uables.</p>
