        <p>the men or the masters acknowledge it or no. Profit-sharing is an acknowledgment of this fact. It is an invitation to the men to think of the influence of their work on the total result, and apply their minds to the increase of the total in which they are entitled to a definite share. If this acknowledgment of the common interest is worked on both sides with fairness and justice it will succeed. If worked by the masters with a view to benefit only or primarily themselves, or by the workers with suspicion and distrust it will fail as it ought to fail. Be this as it may, as far as the gas producing industry is concerned the fact that in thirty towns the principle has been adopted during the last five years is proof that the principle is rapidly spreading and apparently is successful.</p>
